<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">13 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 13 October, from 54 to 1943.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/nero" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nero.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">54 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,972 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nero becomes Roman emperor at 16</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a>, reputedly poisoned by his wife Agrippina, her 16-year-old son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nero">Nero</a> was proclaimed emperor. His reign began promisingly but ended in tyranny, rebellion and his suicide in 68.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">645 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,381 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Taizong abandons the siege of Ansi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With winter approaching and food supplies running out, Emperor Taizong ordered the Tang army to withdraw from its siege of Ansi in the Goguryeo–Tang War. Goguryeo repulsed the first Tang invasions of 645–648.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang">Emperor Taizong of Tang</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1269">1269 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">757 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry III's rebuilt Westminster Abbey is consecrated</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The present church of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westminster-abbey">Westminster Abbey</a>, rebuilt in Gothic style under Henry III from 1245, was consecrated. It replaced the church of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-confessor">Edward the Confessor</a>, consecrated in 1065, where monarchs had been crowned since <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William the Conqueror</a> in 1066.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westminster-abbey">Westminster Abbey</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1307">1307 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">719 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Philip IV of France orders the arrest of the Templars</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In dawn raids across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, Philip IV's officers arrested hundreds of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-templar">Knights Templar</a> on charges of heresy and blasphemy. The heavily indebted king coveted their wealth, and the order was suppressed in 1312.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1479">1479 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">547 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hungarian forces destroy an Ottoman army at Breadfield</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Orăștie in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a>, Hungarian forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-bathory">Stephen Báthory</a> and Paul Kinizsi destroyed a large Ottoman raiding army. It was the greatest Hungarian victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in the reign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matthias-corvinus">Matthias Corvinus</a> and kept Transylvania free of major raids for years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-breadfield">Battle of Breadfield</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1792">1792 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">234 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The cornerstone of the White House is laid</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Freemasons laid the cornerstone of the President's House in the new federal city of Washington. Designed by James Hoban, it has housed every US president since John Adams.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1884">1884 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">142 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Greenwich is chosen as the world's prime meridian</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates at the International Meridian Conference in Washington voted to adopt the meridian through Greenwich as the zero of longitude. The decision underpins maps, navigation and the world's time zones.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1943">1943 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Italy declares war on Germany</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Five weeks after its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pietro-badoglio">Pietro Badoglio</a>'s Italian government declared war on its former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> partner. German forces nonetheless occupied northern and central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> until 1945.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 13 October <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-xiaowen-of-northern-wei"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-xiaowen-of-northern-wei.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emperor Xiaowen of Northern Wei</span><span class="tp">467–499</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/claude-of-france"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/claude-of-france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Claude of France</span><span class="tp">1499–1524</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lillie-langtry"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lillie-langtry.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lillie Langtry</span><span class="tp">1853–1929</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/margaret-thatcher"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Margaret Thatcher</span><span class="tp">1925–2013</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/desi-bouterse"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Desi Bouterse</span><span class="tp">1945–2024</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 13 October <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/robert-i-count-of-flanders"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/robert-i-count-of-flanders.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Robert I, Count of Flanders</span><span class="tp">c. 1035–1093</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/peter-ii-of-cyprus"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/peter-ii-of-cyprus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Peter II of Cyprus</span><span class="tp">c. 1357–1382</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/joachim-murat"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/joachim-murat.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Joachim Murat</span><span class="tp">1767–1815</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/maximilian-i-joseph-of-bavaria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/maximilian-i-joseph-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Maximilian I Joseph of Bavaria</span><span class="tp">1756–1825</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-rwagasore"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-rwagasore.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis Rwagasore</span><span class="tp">1932–1961</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bhumibol-adulyadej"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bhumibol-adulyadej.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bhumibol Adulyadej</span><span class="tp">1927–2016</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
